2595:- Statement: Under TARGETS 1.1 P5: a sweep evaluates release R against WORLD_W0 for every subject in R's scope at one shared basis, in the lane's language, while the writer trace and 64 live readers run; the receipt binds the basis and R's content hash; coverage is exact, every in-scope subject evaluated exactly once with the subject-list hash recorded (NS-P5-COVERAGE); results are published as work items through EP-OUTBOX under the delivery key (id, publication sequence) with early cutoff, so an activation that leaves a payload equal to the latest published one publishes nothing and a return to an earlier payload publishes a new sequence (RULINGS Q36a, Q38f), and equal O-DOMAIN's expected outputs; subjects the driver mutates after the basis is captured keep sweep outputs at the captured basis (NS-P5-POST-CAPTURE-MUTATION). Wall time including evaluation and publication stays within NS-P5-SWEEP-S; live read p99 and writer commit p99 stay within NS-P5-LIVE-READ-P99-RATIO and NS-P5-WRITER-P99-RATIO of their no-sweep values; a throttled variant of about 10 minutes overlaps a real compaction or index rebuild, keeps its basis and never blocks writers (no command waits beyond NS-P1-WRITER-WAIT-MAX-MS; OBS-MAINTENANCE shows the maintenance completing; NS-P5-THROTTLED-COMPACTION).
