2662:- Statement: Story and load: 1% of commits lose their ACK and are retried; mid-run the engine (or QLever broker) is killed and restarted. Checked beyond exact answers: every retry returns the original receipt; no acknowledged commit is lost; readers resume at their pinned bases. Added failure schedule GS-04B-INDEX-PARTITION: the current index's feed consumer is cut for 60 s while the source keeps committing; expected: commits and ACKs continue throughout the outage; on every serving surface the composition claims, native included, reads for which the index is not eligible wait at most 10 ms (COMPOSITION watermarkRouting) then route to the fallback; none answers from the stale index; the receipt measures the fallback share per window and the recovery time until the index is eligible again (RULINGS Q31e). Positive and negative witnesses: GS-04-WITNESS-POS, GS-04-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P2-DUP-RECEIPT-FRACTION, NS-P1-VIOLATIONS-MAX. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.
