18595:      "statement": "Story and load: valid-time corrections 30 days back on 1,000 subjects during live traffic. Checked beyond exact answers: the feed reports the valid-time range; derived state is re-run; explain at the old basis still shows the old belief. Positive and negative witnesses: GS-08-WITNESS-POS, GS-08-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P3-GAPS-MAX, NS-P1-VIOLATIONS-MAX. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.",
18779:      "statement": "Story and load: a new release changes 3 requirements; activation is a fact; the sweep re-reconciles 100k subjects at one pinned basis with live traffic. Checked beyond exact answers: P5 bars hold; in-flight reconciles finish on the old release. Activation is compared with GS.11's preview at one common input basis (GS-10-11-COMMON-BASIS); work items publish under the delivery key (id, publication sequence) with early cutoff (OUTBOX, RULINGS Q38f). Positive and negative witnesses: GS-10-WITNESS-POS, GS-10-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P5-SWEEP-S, NS-P5-LIVE-READ-P99-RATIO, NS-P5-WRITER-P99-RATIO. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.",
18874:      "statement": "Story and load: 'who gains work' for a candidate release over 100k subjects, without applying it, during live traffic. Checked beyond exact answers: identical answer to the post-activation sweep; never blocks writers. The preview is compared with GS.10's activation at one common input basis (GS-10-11-COMMON-BASIS); preview publishes nothing to the outbox. Positive and negative witnesses: GS-11-WITNESS-POS, GS-11-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P1-WRITER-WAIT-MAX-MS, NS-P5-LIVE-READ-P99-RATIO. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.",
18968:      "statement": "Story and load: explain reads at a past basis for 1,000 subjects, repeated three times while writes continue. Checked beyond exact answers: bit-for-bit identical answers modulo erasure across repeats and across lanes (ERASURE reproduction); as-of pull p99 reported. Positive and negative witnesses: GS-12-WITNESS-POS, GS-12-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P1-VIOLATIONS-MAX. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.",
19338:      "statement": "Story and load: erase PII for 10k subjects (crypto-shredding or real deletion) during live traffic. Checked beyond exact answers: reads that start after the erasure publishes return ErasedValue markers at every basis; values are unrecoverable from every PROTECTED_COPY_INVENTORY location; history keeps its shape; explain still works modulo erasure (provisional, flagged for Sam). Positive and negative witnesses: GS-16-WITNESS-POS, GS-16-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P1-READ-P99-256-MS, NS-P3-GAPS-MAX. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.",
19430:      "statement": "Story and load: agents write drafts and proposals at 5x the human rate, most discarded. Checked beyond exact answers: proposals never leak into decisions; pulls at a basis see exactly what was committed. Positive and negative witnesses: GS-17-WITNESS-POS, GS-17-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P4-PULL-P99-MS, NS-P1-VIOLATIONS-MAX. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.",
19616:      "statement": "Story and load: the dependency-index consumer crashes mid-stream and resumes from its checkpoint. Checked beyond exact answers: no gap; zero duplicate externally visible effects throughout, counted by the outbox delivery key (id, publication sequence), with replay attempts allowed and counted; per-subject order kept; catch-up lag measured (RULINGS Q31h, Q36a). Added failure schedule GS-19B-OUTBOX-CRASH: the consumer crashes after delivering an outbox item but before recording completion; expected: the receiver deduplicates by the delivery key (id, publication sequence) of OUTBOX: exactly one externally visible effect per delivery key, and a later return to an earlier payload is a new delivery (RULINGS Q36a, Q38f). Positive and negative witnesses: GS-19-WITNESS-POS, GS-19-WITNESS-NEG. Bars: NS-P3-GAPS-MAX, NS-P3-ORDER-VIOLATIONS-MAX. Expected answers from O-REPLAY (state), O-DOMAIN (domain outputs under WORLD_W0) or O-HAND. The scenario fails on any wrong answer, lost or duplicated commit, feed gap or order violation, or missed bar.",
20390:      "statement": "Long sweeps pin a log position, not a long database transaction. Each engine declares a route for this requirement, NATIVE or WORKAROUND (with its design id and a plain statement of what the engine cannot do natively); the requirement's own CS-REQ tests pass on that route. An open requirement never removes an engine from comparison. Starting points: XTDB: snapshot token or system-time basis; QLever: position in the log; one request per page.",
20534:      "statement": "Every CS-ERASURE boundary, marker and reproduction case per ERASURE: a read that started before the erasure published may return the old value (ER-INFLIGHT-READ); every read that starts after it, at any basis including bases before the erasure, returns ErasedValue {erasedAt} in place of the value (ER-AFTER-PUBLICATION-ALL-BASES), with assertion identities and valid and record intervals unchanged (ER-SHAPE-KEPT); a reader already pinned when the erasure lands follows the same rule (ER-PINNED-READER); an index or cache serves any basis only after applying every published erasure, independently of the basis (ER-FRONTIER-OLD-BASIS), and erasure invalidates every old-basis cache entry holding the value (ER-CACHE-INVALIDATION); expected post-erasure answers come independently from O-REPLAY (ER-ORACLE-POST).",
20782:      "title": "Reads are served only by an index eligible for their basis",
20783:      "statement": "Per COMPOSITION eligibility (RULINGS Q31d): an index serves basis B only when its watermark, a fully resolved prefix, has reached B in B's epoch (CO-EPOCH-MISMATCH), C1's conditions hold, it can reconstruct B (a current-only index only inside the validity interval of every attribute read, CO-RECONSTRUCT-OUTSIDE-VALIDITY) and it has applied every published erasure (CO-ERASURE-FRONTIER); a read with no eligible index waits at most T-WATERMARK-WAIT-MS (CO-WATERMARK-WAIT) and then routes to an eligible fallback (CO-WATERMARK-FALLBACK) whose latency counts in the read's own latency (CO-FALLBACK-LATENCY-COUNTS); the receipt records the route and the surface language, a cross-language fallback is counted per surface (CO-FALLBACK-LANGUAGE), and fallbacks are reported as a share of reads per window (CO-FALLBACK-SHARE, OBS-WATERMARK); no index answers for a basis it is not eligible for (CO-NO-STALE-ANSWER); history and analytics trail asynchronously behind their watermarks (CO-ASYNC-HISTORY).",
20875:      "statement": "Per COMPOSITION ackOwnership (RULINGS Q31e, replacing Q28's ACK clause): the source of truth sends every ACK after its own publication (CO-ACK-AFTER-SOURCE-PUBLICATION, OBS-ACK-ORDER); the pull at the returned position is served by an index eligible for it, else by the fallback, so read-your-own-write is exact (CO-RYOW-ROUTED); during a current-index outage commits and ACKs continue and pulls fall back (CO-OUTAGE-ACKS-CONTINUE), and the index catches up from the feed through a bounded queue (CO-CATCHUP-BOUNDED-QUEUE). Per COMPOSITION fallbackEquivalence (RULINGS Q34b), this holds on every serving surface the composition claims in the lane's language, native included (CO-RYOW-PER-SURFACE); a stale fallback is rejected (CO-STALE-FALLBACK-REJECTED); a cross-language fallback recipe is bound to the same semantic query identity (parameters, basis, meaning) and the same oracle answer (CO-CROSS-LANGUAGE-RECIPE-IDENTITY), with total request latency and language attribution recorded.",
